one of my favorite things about this  movie with you is that you get to do  more stunts so what is something that  might make someone out there go there is  no way she's doing that on her own but  it's actually a stunt that you yourself  are pulling it off um  i actually did a lot of the the fighting  in in the kitchen scene and i really  wanted to like i  like i really wanted to prove to justin  that i that i could do it and and i  trained really hard in order to do it so  so yeah that was that was mostly me i'm  not going to say all me but mostly me  can you tell me a little bit about the  relationship between you the actor and  either your stun double or coordinator  what do you like to get from the stunt  team in order to make you feel super  comfortable and confident when you hit  the set to pull that off um to me it's  like choreography and a dance and with  me it's got to be muscle memory like you  can  give me  direction as much as you want but unless  i have it in my body i won't be able to  do it so  god bless the scent team because i was  meeting them like every day for an hour  and practicing i was like let's go  through it again let's go through it  again let's go through it again and they  were probably so  sick of me by the end but it like that's  what it takes for me to perfect it  so i just need repetition repetition  repetition and um that's really what  makes me feel safe i need to get there  on the day being 100 prepared i can't  you cannot wing it because once they get  the cameras in and you're in the set and  it feels a little bit different  you still have to have it in your body  so that's that's what makes me feel  comfortable so patience is what i need  from them just because now i'm curious  can you compare and contrast that  approach to your approach doing dialogue  heavy scenes do you also like to you  know same thing study and know your  stuff yeah i i have to it's it's similar  to i mean it's the same thing like when  i was in college there were crammers  which i was always like  like how are you able to do that  i'm not like i would have to take like  two hours a night and like  methodically  prepare i was not i was never a crammer  and like  can you imagine cramming an action scene  and being like getting there and being  like what am i what am i doing like like  that to me is like my nightmare so um  so yeah i can compare it to that same  thing with with dialogue you have to  like slowly get it  get it in there and hopefully you have  like a supportive partner like i do who  like constantly runs lines with me  because otherwise you're lost speaking  of supportive partners on set i love  talking about the value of a good scene  partner so whether it's an f9 or any of  the fast movies can you think of an  example of a scene where you were having  a tough time nailing it but your partner  in that scene if not the director pulled  something out of you that you couldn't  access yourself  yeah  um  [Music]  well the scene with paul in five where  i'm petrified of like jumping off the  roof i remember he made me feel really  comfortable and he made me feel like i  could do it um also justin and i have a  shorthand because we've worked together  on annapolis and then on four five  six  and now nine  um  so he knows how to trigger certain  things in me he knows like how to push  my buttons um  so  so yeah  i i trust him completely i fear i'm  getting into too many specifics when you  filmed this forever ago but is there an  example of how justin pushed your  buttons on f9 that kind of like lit a  fire in you  well i think often times with me it's  like  bring up my kid or bring up like how it  relates to that or or bring up um  like sometimes  justin's so funny sometimes he'll just  be like clutch and i'm just like  like it'll be like one word and i'm just  like  yes  um or sometimes it really helps me i'm  very practical it helps me to go behind  the camera and like look at this like  watch myself i'm not one of those actors  that's going to get neurotic and like  i am a neurotic actor but i'm not gonna  like it helps me to watch the  performance and go oh i see i see what's  missing i see what's not connecting  there so um it's really nice when you  work with directors who allow you to do  that this is an f9 specific but someone  recently told me in an interview that  they learned early on that it wasn't  appropriate to ask to look at dailies or  go behind the monitor have you ever been  in that situation where a director is  like i don't want you to see this but  you need to for yourself yeah i have  been in that situation but i also grew  up like on the faculty i remember they  would show dailies during lunch so you  were able to like  watch the dailies or you could like ask  karen makeup like what do they look like  how's it looking like you know or can i  see or oftentimes hair and makeup gets  the dailies and you can like sneak them  like you can you're like show me that  and or you have to know the right person  in the in the crew um  but yeah it's kind of a drag you know  it's a drag when they lie to you and  they're like i'm sorry we don't have  playback and you're just like um that's  a lie  uh  no so yeah it's it's very helpful to me  because i can tweak things and be  objective yeah i feel like i'm very uh  detail-oriented and i like to study so i  can understand that that way of  approaching it totally  so looking ahead a little with f9  jacob is a big motivating factor for mia  to return to the action and the mission  is it safe to assume that family  necessitates her return to that type of  material in the movie going forward i  hope so i think um  you know i would love to explore me and  jacob's relationship further i feel like  i feel like we touched upon the fact  that i was in communication with him  without dom knowing and that's like a  big  betrayal and we never really addressed  it i also  would love to explore like what is my  relationship to jacob  um and i also think you know i have  these like teenage kids that are that  i've that i've  sort of  for lack of a better word quarantined  and are they breaking out or they like  what are they doing because they've got  the toretto blood in them too and so  what does that look like for them  um and how does mia manage that i'd love  to see that dynamic come out as well  bringing up her being in contact with  jacob because i know you like to do your  homework did you ever come up with you  know either like a backstory or a  run-through of how those conversations  went what they talked about and things  like that  i no i think it looked more like  it  i think it looked more like mia  grappling for information or trying  hunting him down trying to find him and  him being really really elusive  and shut down  um i think that's what that looked like  so then what about doing the scene in f9  when you finally see him face to face  because it's like it's on screen for a  split second it doesn't seem a very  telling moment it is and those are the  most like justin loves giving me those  i had one i remember there was like this  massive  scene between um  dwayne johnson and and vin  and i was screaming tom and i'm the one  to like get him to stop just through a  look and i was like justin that's too  much pressure and that's kind of how i  felt like on this  where  with jacob like for a split second like  there's an acknowledgement there and  then he goes away  but i was actually i loved the way it  turned out and  on that i didn't check the monitor and i  just completely trusted justin but i was  you know i think it did speak volumes  and i was really happy  um  but yeah there's so much pressure when  those looks come up because it's like  there's so much to pack into those two  hours of a movie it's powerful it works  thank you  thank you very much huge congratulations  again

